WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.380
An ancient Hindu law book makes a promise:

2
00:00:03.430 --> 00:00:06.760
where women are honoured,
the gods rejoice.

3
00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:11.320
Later, the same book says a woman
should never act independently.

4
00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:13.490
The book is the Manusmriti.

5
00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:16.640
Its rules were written
by men, mostly Brahmin,

6
00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:18.820
for an ideal society.

7
00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:22.230
So what do Hindus make
of a book that says both?

8
00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:25.130
In this mission, you'll
explore stridharma,

9
00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:29.230
a woman's duty, and the place
of marriage in Hindu life.

10
00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:32.770
Then you'll see how the roles
of women and men are changing,

11
00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:35.880
at work, at home and in the temple.

12
00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:40.670
Your mission: find out what Hindus
today make of a book that says both.
